--- (c) VERIFY (live; pg=docker infrastructure-timescaledb-1, broker=docker infrastructure-mosquitto-1) ---
env findings (binaries, not assumptions):
- host TCP 127.0.0.1:1883 reaches NO broker log line: mosquitto.conf binds 1883 to 127.0.0.1 *inside the container netns*, so the published host port is unusable (docker-proxy accepts then drops; paho never gets CONNACK). Host QA MUST use 8883+mTLS. Documented here so nobody re-tries 1883 from host.
- PG TCP password is init-time "example" (container env now says "postgres"; stale). Host QA used postgresql://postgres:example@localhost:5432/iot_data. No committed file contains it.
- broker image has no openssl CLI: command identity key/CSR created with host openssl, CA key read once via docker exec -u 0 cat into /tmp/opencode (600), shredded after use (receipt below).
- paho-mqtt 2.1.0 verifies hostname: server.crt SAN = DNS localhost + IP 10.10.1.114, so MQTT_BROKER must be "localhost" (not 127.0.0.1) under TLS. Code default MQTT_BROKER=localhost already complies.
- publisher bug caught live: first smoke 502 "publish not acknowledged" because QoS1 needs loop_start() for PUBACK; fixed (loop_start/stop), re-verified green.
server: uvicorn app.app:app 127.0.0.1:8007, MQTT_TLS=true PORT=8883 CA=$infra/ca.crt CMD_CERT=$infra/command.crt CMD_KEY=/tmp copy (600, shredded after).

